.TH MINIDEB 1 "2026-11-01" "minideblib 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minideb \- query APT repositories and inspect Debian packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minideb
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B minideb
.B deb
.I DEB_COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B minideb
.B dsc
.I DSC_COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minideb
is the command line front end of the minideblib Python library.
It reads the indexes of APT repositories (Release, Packages, Sources,
Contents and DEP-11 metadata) and inspects
.B .deb
and
.B .dsc
files.
.PP
Repositories are given with
.B \-\-url
or taken from the APT sources configuration.
Only the file hashes listed in Release are checked; the Release or InRelease
signature is
.B not
verified, so repository metadata is unauthenticated.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
The global options may be given before or after the command.
A value given after the command wins, \fB\-v\fR counts add up, and
\fB\-\-url\fR, \fB\-c\fR and \fB\-a\fR given after the command extend the
lists given before it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Repository base URL (repeatable).
Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-sources\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-sources " PATH"
A sources.list or deb822 .sources file, or a directory of them (default:
/etc/apt/sources.list and /etc/apt/sources.list.d).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-component " \fICOMP\fR"
Only read this component (repeatable; default: all).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-arch " \fIARCH\fR"
Only read this architecture (repeatable; default: all).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
Skip the check of index hashes. Without it a SHA256 or stronger hash is
required: an index or \fB.dsc\fR listed only with MD5 or SHA\-1 is rejected.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Write one JSON document to standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Network timeout.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Number of network retries.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log steps to standard error; \fB\-vv\fR also logs requests and details.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Hide warnings (errors are always shown).
.SH COMMANDS
Aliases are given in parentheses.
.TP
.BR suites " (" su ) " [\-\-suite NAME] [\-\-probe WHICH | \-\-no\-probe]"
List suites (probed for \fB\-\-url\fR).
.TP
.BR components " (" comps ) " SUITE"
List the components of a suite.
.TP
.BR archs " (" arch ) " SUITE"
List the architectures of a suite.
.TP
.BR list " (" ls ) " SUITE [\-c COMP]... [\-a ARCH]... [\-\-source]"
List the packages of a suite.
The own options of \fBlist\fR (\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-a\fR), \fBfiles\fR (\fB\-a\fR),
\fBappstream\fR (\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-a\fR) and \fBicons\fR (\fB\-c\fR) are repeatable and
replace the global ones for that command.
.TP
.BR show " (" sh ) " SUITE PACKAGE"
Show the control data of a package.
.TP
.BR versions " (" ver ) " PACKAGE [\-\-suite NAME] [\-\-probe WHICH | \-\-no\-probe]"
Show the versions of a package in all suites.
.TP
.BI \-\-suite " NAME"
(\fBsuites\fR, \fBversions\fR) Probe this extra suite (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-probe " WHICH"
(\fBsuites\fR, \fBversions\fR) Candidate suites to probe for \fB\-\-url\fR, because many
archives do not allow directory listings.
\fIWHICH\fR is \fBall\fR (the default), \fBdebian\fR (stable, stable\-updates,
stable\-backports, testing), \fBubuntu\fR (the latest release and the two latest LTS
releases, each with \-updates, \-security and \-backports) or \fBnone\fR (only the
\fB\-\-suite\fR names).
Probing costs up to two requests (InRelease, then Release) per candidate.
Only used with a single \fB\-\-url\fR; with several \fB\-\-url\fR or with
\fB\-\-sources\fR it is ignored and only the \fB\-\-suite\fR names (or the configured
suites) are used.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-probe
(\fBsuites\fR, \fBversions\fR) Same as \fB\-\-probe none\fR.
.TP
.BR search " (" find ) " SUITE PATTERN"
Search package names and descriptions.
The pattern is a substring, or a glob with * or ? (names only).
.TP
.BR files " (" contents ) " SUITE PATH [\-a ARCH]..."
Find the package providing a file, using the Contents indexes.
These are large downloads; scope them with \fB\-c\fR and \fB\-a\fR.
.TP
.BR appstream " (" as ) " SUITE [\-\-id ID | \-\-package NAME | \-\-search TEXT] [\-\-locale LOC]"
List DEP-11 (AppStream) components.
Needs PyYAML.
\fB\-\-search\fR is a case\-insensitive substring of the id, package, name or summary.
\fB\-\-locale\fR selects the locale for name and summary (default: C).
Exit status 1 when \fB\-\-id\fR or \fB\-\-package\fR matches nothing.
.TP
.B icons SUITE [\-c COMP]...
List DEP-11 icon tarballs (path, icon size, bytes).
.TP
.BR source " (" src ) " SUITE PACKAGE [\-\-version V]"
Show the .dsc of a source package (hash-checked download).
.TP
.B mcp [SERVER OPTIONS]
Run a Model Context Protocol server for AI agents on standard input and output; see
\fBMCP SERVER\fR.
.TP
.B dsc info FILE
Print the key fields of a .dsc file.
.TP
.B dsc files FILE
List the files of a .dsc with size and hashes.
.TP
.B dsc verify FILE [\-\-dir DIR]
Check the size and hashes of the listed files.
Exit status 2 on a mismatch or a missing file.
.TP
.BR "deb info" " (" i ) " FILE"
Print the control fields (like \fBdpkg\-deb \-I\fR).
.TP
.BR "deb ctrl" " (" control ) " FILE DIR"
Extract the control files to DIR (like \fBdpkg\-deb \-e\fR).
Existing regular files are replaced; a symlink as an entry below DIR or as a
directory below DIR is refused (exit status 2).
.TP
.BR "deb ls" " (" list ) " FILE"
List the contents, tar style (like \fBdpkg\-deb \-c\fR).
.TP
.BR "deb extract" " (" x ) " FILE DIR [\-\-max\-size BYTES] [\-\-skip\-absolute\-symlinks]"
Safely extract the data to DIR (like \fBdpkg\-deb \-x\fR).
Paths and links that would leave DIR are refused, and then nothing is extracted.
This includes symlinks with an absolute target, which many packages ship;
\fB\-\-skip\-absolute\-symlinks\fR leaves such links out (with a warning for each) and
extracts the rest.
For \fBdeb ctrl\fR and \fBdeb extract\fR, DIR is created with its missing
parents. DIR itself must not be a symlink; symlinks in the directories leading
to it are followed, as they are chosen by the caller and not by the package.
A local user who can write to a parent of DIR could swap DIR after the check:
extract into a private directory.
.TP
.BR "deb field" " (" f ) " FILE [FIELD...]"
Print fields (like \fBdpkg\-deb \-f\fR).
If a field is missing, the ones found are printed and the exit status is 1.
.SH MCP SERVER
.B minideb mcp
runs a local Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for AI agents.
It speaks JSON\-RPC 2.0 on standard input and output, one message per line, and is
started by the agent's host program.
It works on Linux and macOS only and refuses to start as root (real, effective or saved
user id 0).
Standard output carries protocol messages only; logs go to standard error.
.PP
The global options \fB\-\-url\fR (repeatable), \fB\-\-sources\fR, \fB\-\-no\-verify\fR,
\fB\-\-timeout\fR, \fB\-\-retries\fR, \fB\-v\fR (\fB\-\-verbose\fR),
\fB\-q\fR (\fB\-\-quiet\fR) and \fB\-h\fR (\fB\-\-help\fR) are accepted after \fBmcp\fR.
Repositories given with \fB\-\-url\fR or \fB\-\-sources\fR are named repo1, repo2, ...;
the system sources are \fBnot\fR read, so without them the agent names a repository
URL in each call.
\fB\-\-no\-verify\fR only affects the checks of indexes: downloaded files are always
verified, and a warning is printed at start.
.PP
Tools:
.BR repository_overview ,
.BR search_packages ,
.BR package_versions ,
.BR package_info ,
.BR source_info ,
.BR find_file ,
.BR appstream_components ,
.BR download_package ,
.BR inspect_deb
and
.BR inspect_dsc .
Results are JSON; text taken from a repository is untrusted data.
Without an architecture list the tools cover every architecture of the suite and group
the results; \fBdownload_package\fR fails if several architectures are candidates.
.SS Server options
.TP
.BI \-\-download\-dir " DIR"
Base directory for downloads (default: the directory the server was started in, checked
when a download is requested).
An explicit \fIDIR\fR must exist and be writable; this is checked at start.
Downloads are also allowed in a private per\-session directory (mode 0700) below the
temporary directory, which is not removed at exit.
Existing files are never overwritten and symlinks are never followed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-download
Read\-only server without the \fBdownload_package\fR tool.
.TP
.BI \-\-allow\-host " HOST"
Only accept repositories on this host (repeatable; \fB*.example.org\fR matches
subdomains); \fBfile://\fR mirrors stay allowed.
Default: any host.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-link\-local
Allow link\-local addresses and cloud metadata host names, which are refused by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-response\-bytes " N"
Cap of one tool result message (default: 200000, at least 4096).
Results carry their data twice for newer protocol versions, so about a third is usable.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-download\-bytes " N"
Cap of the total size of the files of one \fBdownload_package\fR call (default: 1 GiB).
.TP
.BI \-\-call\-timeout " SECONDS"
Time limit of one tool call (default: 120, at most 604800).
.TP
.BI \-\-download\-timeout " SECONDS"
Time limit of one \fBdownload_package\fR call (default: 900, at most 604800).
.SS Exit status
The server exits with status 0 at EOF on standard input, and on SIGTERM or SIGINT once
it is running (a signal that arrives while it is still starting gets the default
action), and with status 2 when it cannot start (root, a bad directory or option, an
unsupported platform).
Calls still running or queued at EOF or a signal are cancelled and get no response.
The server waits for them up to 5 seconds and exits at most 7 seconds after a signal;
a second signal exits at once.
.PP
Proxies are taken from \fBhttp_proxy\fR, \fBhttps_proxy\fR and \fBno_proxy\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Nothing found: \fBshow\fR, \fBfiles\fR, \fBversions\fR, \fBsource\fR and \fBsuites\fR
with an empty result, \fBappstream \-\-id\fR/\fB\-\-package\fR matching nothing, and
\fBdeb field\fR with a missing field.
Nothing is written to standard output then (also with \fB\-\-json\fR, except that
\fBdeb field\fR without \fB\-\-json\fR prints the fields it found).
\fBlist\fR and \fBsearch\fR exit with 0 on an empty result.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, network or data error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list
.TQ
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/
Default repository configuration, used when neither \fB\-\-url\fR nor
\fB\-\-sources\fR is given.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
minideb \-\-url http://deb.debian.org/debian components stable
minideb \-\-url http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu list noble \-c main \-a amd64
minideb \-\-url http://deb.debian.org/debian source stable hello
minideb deb info package.deb
minideb dsc verify hello_2.10\-3.dsc
minideb mcp \-\-download\-dir ~/debs
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dpkg\-deb (1),
.BR sources.list (5),
.BR deb822 (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Alexander D. Kanevskiy <kad@bifh.org>
